{"step_index":1530,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T02:13:24Z","input_tokens":2455,"cache_read_tokens":128462,"output_tokens":1060,"thinking":"The mean temperature calculation precisely matches the target temperature with negligible error, confirming the simulation's thermal equilibrium. Kinetic energy, derived from the equipartition theorem, is also in excellent agreement with the theoretical value, validating the simulation's energy distribution.\n\n\nMean total energy is extremely well-conserved with an error of only 0.02 eV, and the minimum gap between slabs is greater than 5.6 Å, confirming no contact occurred. Surface fracture energy at 300 K is calculated, using energy differences between bulk and unrelaxed slab models, resulting in 2.3475 J/m². This calculated value matches the 0 K result and existing literature values from Rauls et al. 1999 within 0.1% error.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ls -la /home/WORKSTATION4WSL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/mdi_workspace_backup/aimd_2H-SiC_10-10_8periods_vac3.0A_unrelaxed_300K_400steps_rtx5080/*.png","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"List PNG graphs in unrelaxed 400-step slab directory"}}]}
